# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository policy
#
# Tracked: C/C++ sources and headers (core/, client/, network/, tests/),
# CMake build files, GLSL shader sources, asset-generation and export scripts,
# documentation, aircraft definitions and manifests, physics tables and this
# file.
#
# Not tracked: build trees, dependency caches, compiler output, Blender
# sources, runtime 3D models, large textures, generated screenshots, validation
# videos, temporary logs and other generated validation artifacts. See
# docs/ASSETS.md for how to obtain or regenerate the excluded runtime content.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Research-only third-party documents and images are kept locally.
/reference/

# Build trees
/build*/
/.cache/

# Dependency caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
vcpkg_installed/
/.vcpkg-cache/
/CMakeUserPresets.json

# Compiler and linker outputs
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.gch

# Generated shader binaries. GLSL sources and pack_shaders.py are tracked.
*.spv

# Blender sources and autosave backups. The aircraft models are rebuilt from
# scripts/ and the reference material; no .blend is version controlled.
*.blend
*.blend1
*.blend2

# Runtime 3D models. These are large generated binaries, rebuilt by the
# export scripts in scripts/ from the documented authoring pipeline.
*.glb
*.gltf

# Large textures (1 MiB and above). Editable source textures below this
# threshold stay tracked; runtime ships them embedded in the LOD models.
assets/typhoon/textures/fuselage_base.png
assets/typhoon/textures/fuselage_mr.png
assets/typhoon/textures/tail_base.png
assets/typhoon/textures/wings_base.png
assets/typhoon/textures/wings_mr.png
assets/aircraft/sr71/textures/sr71_fuselage_4k_basecolor.png
assets/aircraft/sr71/textures/sr71_nacelle_2k_basecolor.png
assets/aircraft/sr71/textures/sr71_wing_4k_basecolor.png

# Generated screenshots. Canonical validation captures are produced locally by
# scripts/capture_*.py and scripts/benchmark_*.py.
docs/images/
output/**/*.png
output/**/*.jpg
output/**/*.jpeg
output/**/*.ppm

# Validation videos
*.mp4
*.webm
*.mkv
*.mov
*.avi

# Temporary logs
*.log
*.tmp

# Third-party colour-management configuration. These are OCIO/ACES configs, LUTs
# and ICC profiles supplied by the local Blender/colour pipeline, not project
# source, and they carry their own upstream licences.
output/color_management/

# Extensionless helper binaries built from the .cpp files beside them. Only the
# sources are tracked; these are debug-info ELF executables.
output/m3_68/inspect_gear
output/m3_68/measure_assets

# Generated validation artifacts: test transcripts, measurement reports,
# manifests, telemetry CSVs and render benchmarks. Retained locally as the
# evidence behind the validation documents, which cite them in prose rather
# than linking them. These are scoped by extension rather than by excluding
# the output/ directory, because git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded; that keeps the hand-written helper sources
# (comparison_probe.cpp, inspect_gear.cpp, measure_assets.cpp) tracked.
output/**/*.txt
output/**/*.json
output/**/*.csv

# Local editor and OS state
/imgui.ini
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# M3.68.1 generated test transcripts, JUnit and diagnostics
output/m3_68_1/

# Generated M3.7 measurements, parser/impairment evidence and JUnit transcripts
output/m3_7/

# Generated M3.7.1 measurements, baseline comparison builds and JUnit
output/m3_7_1/

# Generated M4 measurements, baseline builds, JUnit and screenshots
output/m4/

# Launcher runtime state; release products remain under build/.
/.installation.lock
/last-update-result.json
